WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.036
-Also, it is a very
exciting week

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.937
for us here at "Late Night"
because Fred Armisen

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:08.607
is back with us on the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.910
-And, Fred,
I share this

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.278
with the audience
any time you're here.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.648
I am always overwhelmed
by how many different projects

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.450
you have going at one time,

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.152
and then you also
do things not for you,

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:22.688
not to enrich yourself
financially or artistically,

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.190
but for other people.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.626
And I heard you're doing
an incredible thing.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.129
You are counterprogramming
Halloween for kids

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.332
who don't like trick
or treating.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.767
-Finally, yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.736
-So I'm doing something
where kids

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:41.207
can start rehearsing
for other holidays.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:44.144
Like, you know,
Christmas or Hanukkah

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.745
or Easter or whatever it is,

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.114
they could start
just doing a rehearsal

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.049
just to get ready
for birthdays and things.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.885
The problem is
kids aren't ready.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.786
-Okay.
-So we bring them --

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.055
-They, like, sort of get
caught off guard, say, by like,

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.191
hey, it's Thanksgiving.
And they're like...

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.693
-Yes, that's exactly
what I mean.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.894
So, like, let's sit
around a table,

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.229
let's have imaginary food.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.131
Let's kind of like
go through it

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.834
so you're not nervous about it,
and it goes for birthdays, too.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.502
Do you know how to say
happy birthday to someone?

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.703
Do you know how to like...?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.971
-Oh, so it's not
just for your birthday,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.672
but if you get invited
to a birthday,

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:14.841
you can rehearse for that.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.342
-It just takes away
the nervousness.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.543
-Yeah.
-So when they come --

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.612
-This is something that you're
doing uniquely

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.847
on October 31st,

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.114
if you don't want
to trick or treat,

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:24.384
you go to --
where do you go?

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.152
-So, it's in Central Park.
-Okay.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.254
-And so there's a --
there's like all these

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.791
bicycle rentals there,
and it's just right next to it.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.993
But please don't crowd in
because all the tourists

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.695
are trying to grab the bicycles.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:38.130
So we're just asking everyone
to like please, please,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:41.133
please move over.
There's like an area

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.503
that has like a little bit
of grass and cement.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.937
Please don't crowd the bicycles.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.372
We're just asking.
-Now, why?

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.207
You seem so concerned
about crowding

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.343
the bicycle rack,
why would you do it?

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.146
Why would you set up there?
Because you're almost talking

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.048
more about the bicycle
rack situation

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.883
than you are about
the actual holiday rehearsal.

00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.485
-It's just because
they get so mad.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.287
The people who rent out
the bikes are always kind of

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.688
like they take it out on me

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.190
and they start yelling at me
about it,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.426
and I'm like, I can't hand--
You know, these are kids.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:08.861
You know what I mean?

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.596
So kids, they
just wander around,

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.031
and we're just asking, please,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.934
just stay on the cement,
just stay on the pavement

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.636
and we could do
the rehearsals from there.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.837
-Okay, great.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.405
And if people
want to learn more about this,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.806
is there a website
they can go to?

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:22.775
-No, but I asked them
to talk to you.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.545
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.113
-Give it up for
Fred Armisen, everybody.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.781
-Thank you.
Thank you.

